ight where it began everything  would be back in place nothing really  ever happened  in a superman comic which i realized  after reading you know 100 or so of them  uh you could read them in any order  because uh  they had to template and nothing was  ever going to happen you know  jimmy olsen might become a giant  turtleman and during the course of the  adventure but by the end of the  adventure he would be back to being  jimmy olsen again  there was no permanent changes and then  stan lee came along with marvel  and it was the characters were fighting  in the fantastic four  the thing didn't like being the thing  and was constantly fighting with johnny  storm and they didn't have secret  identities their identities were  were out there and then spider-man came  along and  and you know spider-man he didn't have  his lowest lane he had a series of  girls he had liz allen at first who we  had the hots for  but she she preferred to bully flash  thompson and he couldn't get anywhere  with her  and then he took up with an older woman  betty brandt who was dave jonas  secretary and uh he had that  relationship for a while and he took up  with gwen stacy  that didn't work out and get it well  she died yeah that was that was  traumatic but she actually died  yeah you know i mean dc never killed  lois lane or  or even jimmy olsen although you might  have wanted to  [Laughter]  nothing ever happened in the dc's and a  lot was happening in marvel you didn't  know who was safe  and you didn't know what would what  would actually happen and time passed  i went believe it or not looking at the  old  daughter you see and have before you i  went to high school with peter parker  we were both in high school when i  started reading spider-man comics  and just about the same time we both  graduated high school and went to  college  and i went to northwestern and you know  i'm in a different city  i'm making new friends i got a roommate  that i didn't know before  i'm taking new classes it's adjusting to  a whole new war peter parker went  through the same stuff  you know he went to college and he had a  he didn't go as far away from home  he just but he did have to move out of  the house with aunt may things happened  and  and that was amazing and another one of  my comic book  letters i published a number of letters  was a letter to the avengers um  which again was published and it was  about the issue it was about avengers  number nine i think it was which is the  intro that  introduced wonder man i'm not sure any  of you remember this you're  probably all too young you probably  don't even remember wonder man but  wonder man came in and he joined the  avengers and he was a brand new hero  and he really wasn't a hero  he was a spy who set to join the  avengers to  destroy them from within so he only was  playing to be a hero but he was actually  going to destroy them from within  but then he became friendly with them  and he couldn't bring himself to destroy  them from within  so he betrayed his masters and  they killed him so he died in the same  issue that he was introduced in  and i love this of course that i wrote a  long letter  about how great this was and i look back  now and i  you know like my whole career is based  on on avengers number nine i mean  introducing these gray characters who  have divided loyalties who  are not what they seem i'm a little  traumatized  and then killing them unexpectedly yeah  yeah  now of course it was comics so they  brought wonderment back eventually but  uh  that that's the big flaw with comics and  uh i try never to bring anyone back  or if i do they're they're really  screwed up mm-hmm
 

